      "text_raw": "Such a bandgap reference\nbased on two current mir-\nrors has two operating\npoints. A zero current is also\nperfectly possible. This cir-\ncuit does not start by itself.\nThe two operating points\nare found by plotting the\ntwo currents versus the\ncommon voltage V . The\nBE1\ncurrent of transistor Q2 is\nmore linear as it has a feed-\nback resistor R .\n2\nThe top current mirror\nhas unity gain. The operat-\ning points are now found at the crossings of the lines.\nZero current works as well as the required operating point.\nStartup circuits are therefore required.",
      "text": "Such a bandgap reference based on two current mirrors has two operating points. A zero current is also perfectly possible. This circuit does not start by itself. The two operating points are found by plotting the two currents versus the common voltage V . The BE1 current of transistor Q2 is more linear as it has a feedback resistor R . 2 The top current mirror has unity gain. The operating points are now found at the crossings of the lines. Zero current works as well as the required operating point. Startup circuits are therefore required."
